 D: 984 6689 7972\nPasscode: 825952\n\nThe Department of Anesthesiology\, P
 erioperative & Pain Medicine invites colleagues across the University to i
 ts Evening Edition Grand Rounds on Monday\, November 16\, featuring Diana 
 E. Ramos\, MD\, MPH\, MBA\, California’s first Latina Surgeon General.\n
 \nDr. Ramos will present “Beyond the Operating Room: Adverse Childhood E
 xperiences\, Maternal Health\, and the Role of Anesthesiology in Preventio
 n.” The talk examines how adverse childhood experiences and toxic stress
  shape health across the lifespan — including implications for pregnancy
 \, maternal health\, and perioperative care — and reviews maternal morbi
 dity and mortality trends and disparities in California\, with attention t
 o where prevention and early intervention can change outcomes. She will al
 so discuss trauma-informed care and opportunities for collaboration across
  care settings.\n\nA board-certified OB-GYN with more than 30 years in pra
 ctice\, Dr. Ramos previously led chronic disease prevention at the Califor
 nia Department of Public Health. Hosted by Brian Bateman\, MD\, MSc\, MBA\
 , The Anesthesiology\, Perioperative and Pain Medicine Endowed Professor a
 nd Chair.\n\n\nNote the early start time. Food served from 5:00 p.m.\; lec
 ture 5:15–6:00 p.m. In person at Assembly Hall\, 500 Pasteur Dr. (3rd Fl
 oor Rooftop)\, or join by Zoom. CME credit available.\n\nWebsite: https://
 med.stanford.edu/anesthesia/education/grand-rounds.html\nQuestions: anesth
